<article class="env-remark" id="06MX">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06MX">Remark <span data-tag="06MX">8.6.8.9</span> <span class="named">(Representable Functors)</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a right fibration of $\infty $-categories and let $\mathscr {F} = \operatorname{Tr}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}/\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{\operatorname{op}} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$ be its contravariant transport representation. Then the functor $\mathscr {F}$ is representable (in the sense of Variant <a data-tag="038B" href="/tag/038B">5.6.6.2</a>) if and only if the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ has a final object. More precisely, $\mathscr {F}$ is representable by an object $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ if and only if $C$ can be lifted to a final object of the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$. See Proposition <a data-tag="02J8" href="/tag/02J8">5.6.6.21</a>. </p>
</article>
